## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1**: Should rejected/rolled-back patches be retried with a different model, or should they be left for manual fixing? Retrying with a fallback model could help, but it also risks generating another bad patch.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2**: For the post-patch verification, should we also re-run the Semgrep scanner on the file (slower but more thorough), or just the built-in regex scanner (faster)?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3**: Some patches in the output were applied even though the council **REJECTED** them (e.g., patches #43 and #44 for Command Injection — both rejected by council reviewers but applied anyway because the user typed "y"). Should we **block** application of council-rejected patches entirely, or keep the current behavior where the user can override?

